-- lib/kernel.cub — the machine, written in the language (part of machine-in-hyperactive).
-- One rule: an eliminator meets a value, and the calculus (nk-act, a table) says what is built on
-- the wires the two held. Everything else is not about any particular calculus: a wire is a slot;
-- a step asks for changes to wires (NkCh); a value with parts is held once and read by reference;
-- an eliminator meeting a blocked value becomes a blocked value; quotation reads a value back as a
-- body. A new type former is rows of the table and bodies written with nk-con and nk-op: no rule,
-- no proof. The executor (NkExec) is outside: it chooses which wire steps next and hands out names.
-- It loads after the library: the proofs use its lemmas on word equality, and the C experiment
-- that emits it is the library's.
import "library.cub"

